<details><summary>Reveal the eleven-vertex calculation</summary>

For triples and five-sets, each constraint has $ inom{5}{3}=10$ variables. On eleven vertices there are $ inom{11}{5}=462$ constraints, and $462<2^9=512$. Therefore a coloring exists with no monochromatic five-set.

</details>

## Dependence is geometry

Two candidate sets meeting in $t$ vertices share exactly $ inom{t}{r}$ colored variables. Explore this rigid overlap, which points toward the [Lovász local lemma](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lov%C3%A1sz_local_lemma) and the [Johnson scheme](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnson_scheme).

